    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Mason Estates are delighted to present this unique 2 bedroom end of terrace period property located just off Clonliffe Road.\n \nAccommodation comprises of an entrance porch, sittingroom, diningroom, kitchen and shower room. Upstairs there are 2 bedrooms. The attic has also been converted into a storage room.\n\nConveniently located within a stroll of Drumcondra Village and within easy reach of the City Centre, M50 Motorway and Dublin Airport.\n\nNo. 3 has every amenity on your doorstep including schools, shops, restaurants and transport links including Drumcondra Train Station.\n\nGENERAL POINTS, SERVICES & UTILITIES:\n•BER is G and BER number is 119720522.\n•Mix of double glazed timber windows and uPVC windows.\n•No heating systems\nOn street residential disk parking. \n\nOUTSIDE: \nOn-street residential disk parking to the front of the property. Side pedestrian access leads to a private rear garden which is approximately 100 feet in length. The rear garden is laid in lawn and has an array of plants and shurbs.\n\nVIEWING: By Appointment Only\n\nNEGOTIATOR: Siobhan Foley MSCSI MRICS\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "ENTRANCE PORCH:\nWith tiled floor.\n\nSITTINGROOM: 3.3m x 4.1m\nThis front reception room oozes with natural light through the original shop front windows. Timber floor.\n\nDININGROOM: 3.1m x 3.5m\nRear reception room with feature timber fireplace with gas fire insert. Fitted storage presses.\n\nKITCHEN: 3.6m x 3.1m (max measurements)\nLocated to the rear of the property with door to rear garden.\n\nSHOWER ROOM: 2.2m x 2.1m\nWith 3 piece suite comprising of w.c., wash hand basin and shower with Triton shower. Door to rear garden. Timber panelled walls and ceiling.\n\nUPSTAIRS:\n\nBEDROOM 1: 2.7m x 4.2m\nDouble bedroom to the front of the property with castiron fireplace with tiled hearth. Original timber floor.\n\nBEDROOM 2: 3.1m x 3.7m\nDouble bedroom to the rear of the property with original timber floor and castiron fireplace.\n\nATTIC ROOM: 4.0m x 4.0m\nWith timber floor.\n\nFLOOR AREA:\nApproximately 67 sq.m. (not including attic space)\n\nNotice\nPlease note we have not tested any apparatus, fixtures, fittings, or services. Interested parties must undertake their own investigation into the working order of these items. All measurements are approximate and photographs provided for guidance only."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li> Excellent location. </li><li> Origianl shop front which is retained from when the property was built in c. 1929. </li><li> Ideally located within a stroll of Drumcondra Village and a range of schools, restaurants & shops. </li><li> Good transport links to the city centre. </li><li> Side pedestrian access to rear garden. </li><li> Private rear garden. </li><li> Many of the period features are retained.</li></ul>"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "BER Details",
        "SortOrder": 4,
        "Content": "BER: G<br>BER No: 119720522<br>Energy Performance Indicator: 727.47 kWh/m2/yr"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Directions",
        "SortOrder": 5,
        "Content": "Travelling along Dorset Street from the City Centre. Continue onto the Drumcondra Road and take the right hand turn at the traffic lights onto Clonliffe Road. Take the first right hand turn onto Saint Georges Avenue and No. 3 is on the right hand side just before the railway line."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Negotiator",
        "SortOrder": 10,
        "Content": "Siobhan Foley"
      }
